openui-bundle.min.js and openui-styles.css are the unmodified files from the
published archive. The JS includes React, ReactDOM, the OpenUI Lang renderer,
the default chat component library, and their runtime dependencies. The package
declares @openuidev/react-lang ^1.0.1 and @openuidev/react-ui ^0.18.1. Its actual
browser export reports React 19.2.4. No package install scripts were run.

Public global: window.__OpenUI
Exports: React, createRoot, Renderer, openuiChatLibrary.

system-prompt.txt was generated from this exact browser bundle in an isolated
Electron page by calling:
  window.__OpenUI.openuiChatLibrary.prompt({bindings: true, toolCalls: false})
This enables reactive variables and local Set/Reset actions. Query/Mutation
instructions are omitted until the host supplies its own authorized tool bridge.
The prompt is a tool-specific resource to load on demand, not a global prompt
to insert into every model request. It describes this bundle's default library,
not the distinct custom library in thesysdev/open-intelligent-ui.

Renderer properties used by the host:
  response, library, isStreaming, initialState, onStateUpdate, onAction, onError.
Continue-conversation actions report type, humanFriendlyMessage, params.context,
and formState; formName is included when the action belongs to a form.

Runtime telemetry: upstream lang-core explicitly excludes browser and browser
worker environments. Server telemetry is opt-in; OPENUI_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1
also disables it if a server integration is added later. This vendored browser
renderer does not use OpenUI Gateway/Cloud. A hidden Electron page verified
local reactive updates and action callbacks with zero HTTP(S) requests.

